{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZstHRU93AN6eH6auVBc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I now have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me summarize:\n\n**Requirement restated:** Implement `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` to allow customers to cancel ACTIVE orders while maintaining atomicity with shipment cascade cancellation, reject conflicts when shipments are CONFIRMED, support idempotent retries, and reject shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity: `Order.kt:11` — currently has no status field\n- OrderRepository: `OrderRepository.kt:11` — in-memory ConcurrentHashMap, basic CRUD\n- OrderController: `OrderController.kt:17` — POST/GET endpoints\n- Shipment entity: `Shipment.kt:9` — already has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentRepository: `ShipmentRepository.kt:11` — in-memory, lacks findByOrderId method\n- ShipmentController: `ShipmentController.kt:22` — create doesn't check order status\n- Error handling: ApiExceptions.kt:11, ApiError.kt:31 (ErrorCode enum), GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n2. Consistent error envelope: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`\n3. In-memory repositories with ConcurrentHashMap\n4. Tests use MockMvc, verify both status and response body structure, clear repos in @BeforeEach\n5. The pattern: data class entities, repository layer for storage, controller layer that throws exceptions\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — must add OrderStatus enum and status field (domain model)\n2. `OrderRepository.kt` — no changes required (existing methods suffice)\n3. `OrderController.kt` — must add cancel endpoint, modify create to initialize ACTIVE status, inject ShipmentRepository\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — must add findByOrderId method (to find shipments for cascade)\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` — must check order status before creating shipment\n6. `ApiError.kt` — must add ORDER_CANCELLED error code (for shipment rejection)\n7. OrderControllerTest — must add cancel endpoint test cases\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Atomicity violation if shipment check and cancellation aren't atomic within a transaction\n2. Race condition if another request modifies order/shipments during cancel\n3. Cascade cancellation must update all CREATED shipments but leave others untouched\n\n**Open questions:** None — all cases are clearly specified.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values, and add a `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**: No changes needed; existing save/findById methods work for our use case.\n\n3. **OrderController.kt**: \n   - Inject `ShipmentRepository` via constructor\n   - Modify `create()` to pass `status = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` when creating Order\n   - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n     - Throws 404 if order doesn't exist\n     - Checks if ANY shipment is CONFIRMED; if yes, throws 409 and changes nothing\n     - Otherwise, updates order status to CANCELLED\n     - Cancels all CREATED shipments\n     - Returns the updated order with 200\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: \n   - Inject `OrderRepository`\n   - In `create()`, after checking shipment ID uniqueness, check if the order is CANCELLED\n   - If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with code ORDER_CANCELLED and 409 status\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**: Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest**: Add test cases for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments (succeeds, cancels shipments)\n   - Cancelling an already-CANCELLED order (idempotent success)\n   - Cancelling when a CONFIRMED shipment exists (409 conflict, nothing changes)\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order (404 not found)\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- I considered making cancel return 204 No Content instead of 200 with body, but the requirement explicitly states \"returns the order\", so 200 with body is correct.\n- I considered adding a OrderService layer for business logic, but the existing codebase puts logic directly in controllers, so I'll follow that pattern.\n- I considered using transactions or atomic operations, but the in-memory repository doesn't support them and the requirement doesn't mandate them. I'll implement it as: get order, check all shipments first, then update if checks pass (all-or-nothing within request scope).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (cancel ACTIVE order)**:\n   - Client: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n   - OrderController: Get order from repo, check status (ACTIVE), check shipments\n   - ShipmentRepository: Find all shipments for order O-1\n   - Check: All shipments are CREATED or CANCELLED (no CONFIRMED)\n   - Update: Order status → CANCELLED, update each CREATED shipment → CANCELLED\n   - Response: 200 OK with updated Order\n\n2. **Idempotent cancel (already CANCELLED)**:\n   - Client: POST /orders/O-2/cancel\n   - OrderController: Get order, status is CANCELLED\n   - Check: Any CONFIRMED? No\n   - Result: No changes needed, return order as-is, 200 OK\n\n3. **Conflict (CONFIRMED shipment exists)**:\n   - Client: POST /orders/O-3/cancel\n   - OrderController: Get order, status ACTIVE\n   - Check shipments: Find one CONFIRMED shipment\n   - Throw: ConflictException(ORDER_SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED) → 409, nothing changes\n   - Response: 409 CONFLICT with error envelope\n\n4. **Not found**:\n   - Client: POST /orders/unknown/cancel\n   - OrderController: Get order → null\n   - Throw: ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND) → 404\n   - Response: 404 NOT FOUND with error envelope\n\n5. **Create shipment for cancelled order**:\n   - Client: POST /shipments with orderId of CANCELLED order\n   - ShipmentController: Check order status\n   - Check: Order exists and is CANCELLED\n   - Throw: ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED) → 409\n   - Response: 409 CONFLICT with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test: Cancelling ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments → order CANCELLED, shipments CANCELLED, 200\n2. Test: Cancelling already CANCELLED order → unchanged, 200 (idempotent)\n3. Test: Cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment → 409, no changes to order or shipments\n4. Test: Cancelling non-existent order → 404 with error envelope\n5. Test: Creating shipment for cancelled order → 409 with error envelope\n6. Test: Creating shipment for non-existent order → still succeeds (current behavior preserved)\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2324,"cache_read_input_tokens":19597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2324},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8de7f2e8-eabc-4a0b-ad13-4e40d245fc26","uuid":"3cb6872b-d8a8-4aa4-9c36-2a6039b9be08","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:42:09.551Z","request_id":"req_011CfZstH2eKWwXWe9kmsy4H"}
