ry.kt** ✅ Required\n   - Added `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method\n   - Rationale: Needed to find shipments when cancelling an order\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** ✅ Required\n   - Added `OrderRepository` injection\n   - Added check in `create()` to reject CANCELLED orders with 409\n   - Rationale: Prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** ✅ Required\n   - Added `ORDER_SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED` error code\n   - Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code\n   - Rationale: Support new error scenarios\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** ✅ Required\n   - Added 5 new tests covering all requirements\n   - Tests: cancel active with shipments, idempotent cancel, conflict on CONFIRMED, 404 on unknown, new order is ACTIVE\n   - Rationale: Test new functionality\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** ✅ Required\n   - Added 2 new tests\n   - Tests: reject shipment for cancelled order, allow for non-existent order\n   - Rationale: Test shipment creation validation\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements addressed.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint allowing customers to cancel ACTIVE orders with proper status tracking, cascade shipment cancellation, idempotent retry support, and appropriate error responses for conflicts and not-found cases.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt — Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE/CANCELLED) and status field to Order entity\n- OrderController.kt — Added cancel endpoint, injected ShipmentRepository, implemented atomicity check and cascade cancellation\n- ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findByOrderId method to locate shipments for an order\n- ShipmentController.kt — Injected OrderRepository, added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- ApiError.kt — Added ORDER_SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt — Added 5 tests covering cancel scenarios (active, idempotent, conflict, not found, new order status)\n- ShipmentControll